From: Sergey Senozhatsky <senozhatsky@chromium.org>
Subject: [PATCH] zram: zstd: skip unused empty compression dictionaries

Do not create compression/decompression dictionaries when no dictionary
was configured. The no-dictionary path uses its embedded contexts and
never reads the dictionary objects allocated during parameter setup.

Adapted from upstream v7 06/15, with the no-dictionary return before
computing dictionary-specific compression parameters. Match the consumers
that select the dictionary path by dict_sz alone.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261025021839.1542805-7-senozhatsky@chromium.org/
Signed-off-by: Sergey Senozhatsky <senozhatsky@chromium.org>
Signed-off-by: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/block/zram/backend_zstd.c b/drivers/block/zram/backend_zstd.c
--- a/drivers/block/zram/backend_zstd.c
+++ b/drivers/block/zram/backend_zstd.c
@@ -72,6 +72,9 @@
 
 	zp->custom_mem.customAlloc = zstd_custom_alloc;
 	zp->custom_mem.customFree = zstd_custom_free;
+
+	if (!params->dict_sz)
+		return 0;
 
 	prm = zstd_get_cparams(params->level, PAGE_SIZE,
 			       params->dict_sz);
